00:02:16.954 --> 00:02:18.870
MARK MANDEL: I really
like Deployment Manager.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.953
So if you're not familiar
with Deployment Manager,

00:02:20.953 --> 00:02:23.540
it's a way to declaratively
basically specify

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.120
the infrastructure you're
on on Google Cloud Platform.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.930
I was super happy to
see that recently they

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.061
have support now for Pub/Sub.

00:02:31.061 --> 00:02:33.060
So if you want to create
topics or subscriptions

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.510
within Deployment Manager, you
can do that through that now.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.440
You couldn't before, which
is really, really cool.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.370
Pub/Sub is a tool that I love.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.810
It's a messaging published
subscribe service that we run.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.750
It's super, super powerful, and
lets you build some really nice

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.734
distributed systems.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:48.650
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.420
That is actually really cool
because it was the last steps

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.270
so we could get rid of our
deploy script for Cloud Spin.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:58.540
Now everything can
actually be done

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.350
